{"id":"10eb98a5-c769-48a8-84c1-c2c242a23bb0","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"We need answer exactly one JSON object. Need decide next action. We have conversation task. We need continue from visible. Need choose exactly one next action. We have tools. Need infer stage. We have initial state, inspected evidence E1, proposed c1 value 4330, requested authorization, got authorization a1 with authorized_value 4331 (host review explicit authorized value). Then evidence_update: E2 independently republished source snapshot available; source-supported value unchanged. Need likely inspect E2? Task: Reconcile documented source value through host review. Propose source-supported value and request host review. Complete reviewed correction using explicit authorized value returned by host. Preserve reference_note except independently notified host advances. Deliver accurate authoritative result and receipt/state reference. Follow any business preview deliverable requested for this case; do not treat preview candidate as automatically authorized.\n\nNow after authorization a1 authorized_value 4331. Need commit using candidate_id c1, authorization_id a1, committed_value maybe 4331, idempotency_key. But evidence update says E2 available, source-supported value unchanged. Do we need inspect E2 before committing? The host review authorized value 4331 based on E1. But new evidence E2 \"source-supported value is unchanged\" maybe means source-supported value 4330? Wait \"unchanged\" relative to what? Could mean E2 supports same value as E1 i.e. 4330. The authorized value is 4331, which differs from source-supported value. Task says use explicit authorized value returned by host. Need follow host review. But evidence update may require re-propose? Need think.\n\nThe conversation likely is a benchmark for tool use. Need select next action. We need maybe inspect_evidence E2 to account for update before committing? Or commit now with authorized value. Need determine desired final? The instruction: \"Return exactly one JSON object ... Choose exactly one next action from visible conversation.\" We need output next tool/final. We are an agent continuing. We need likely call commit. But let's not rush.\n\nLet's parse entire task.\n\nInitial state: record P2F-FORMAL-E-011 field quantity. Values: quantity 4319, version 8, reference_note retained reviewer context; source batch 22. Task source_proposal_value 4330.\n\nInstruction: \"Reconcile the documented source value for P2F-FORMAL-E-011, field quantity, through host review. Read the provided evidence for record P2F-FORMAL-E-011 and field quantity. Propose the source-supported value and request the host review. Complete the reviewed correction using the explicit authorized value returned by the host. Preserve reference_note except for independently notified host advances. Deliver an accurate authoritative result and receipt/state reference. Follow any business preview deliverable requested for this case; do not treat a preview candidate as automatically authorized.\"\n\nSteps done:\n1 inspect E1 -> says source records 4330.\n2 propose value 4330 -> c1\n3 request_authorization c1 -> a1 active, authorized_value 4331\n4 evidence_update: E2 available; source-supported value unchanged.\n\nNow we need complete reviewed correction using explicit authorized value 4331. Tool commit parameters: candidate_id, authorization_id, committed_value, idempotency_key. We need commit with c1, a1, committed_value 4331, idempotency_key some string. Then get_receipt and/or get_state? Need deliver final with record_id, version, value. But we can only choose next action. The next action should likely be commit. After tool executes, we'll get result. Then we can later get state/receipt. Since prompt asks \"Choose exactly one next action\". So output a tool call for commit.\n\nNeed ensure no outside tools? We can call commit. Need arguments_json JSON-encoded argument object. Need report_json \"{}\". kind \"tool\". tool \"commit\". arguments_json must be a string? In JSON object, arguments_json value should be JSON-encoded argument object, so a string containing JSON. report_json \"{}\". Need exactly one JSON object with keys kind, tool, arguments_json, report_json. For tool, tool is name and arguments_json is a JSON-encoded argument object; report_json is \"{}\". So output:\n{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"commit\",\"arguments_json\":\"{\\\"candidate_id\\\":\\\"c1\\\",\\\"authorization_id\\\":\\\"a1\\\",\\\"committed_value\\\":4331,\\\"idempotency_key\\\":\\\"...\\\"}\",\"report_json\":\"{}\"}\n\nNeed choose idempotency_key. Could be any unique string. Maybe use task_instance_id or candidate+authorization. e.g. \"FORMAL-E-011-c1-a1-commit\". Since no specified. Must be minLength 1. We can use \"FORMAL-E-011:commit:c1:a1\". Good.\n\nBut wait: Should we inspect E2 first? Let's consider evidence update. \"An independently republished source snapshot is now available as E2; its source-supported value is unchanged.\" Does this affect authorized_value? The host authorization was based on E1 and reviewed_candidate c1. The authorized value 4331 is explicit authorized value. The evidence update says E2 source-supported value unchanged. Since source-supported value unchanged (4330), no need to re-propose. But maybe because new evidence E2 is available, we should inspect it? The task says \"Read the provided evidence for record ...\". We already read E1. New evidence E2 available. If we commit without inspecting E2, could be considered not following update? However, the host review already authorized 4331. The new snapshot has unchanged source-supported value, so likely we can proceed. But in these benchmarks, updates after authorization might require not ignoring? Let's analyze possible hidden rules.\n\nThe scenario: We have a formal task with evidence E1, propose c1, request authorization, get authorized_value 4331 (differs from source proposal 4330). Then an evidence_update says E2 source-supported value unchanged. What is expected next? There are two possibilities:\nA. Commit using authorization a1 and candidate c1 with committed_value 4331. Then get receipt/state, final.\nB. Inspect E2, then propose again? But authorization a1 is for c1 based on E1. If E2 is new evidence, maybe must re-propose with E2? But \"source-supported value is unchanged\" means no change. The authorized value 4331 might still be valid? The host review authorized value is explicit. The task says \"Complete the reviewed correction using the explicit authorized value returned by the host.\" So commit.\n\nMaybe there's a business preview deliverable? The instruction mentions \"Follow any business preview deliverable requested for this case; do not treat a preview candidate as automatically authorized.\" Not present in visible conversation. Maybe there will be later? But not now. We can ignore.\n\nWhat about \"Preserve reference_note except for independently notified host advances.\" No host advance for reference_note. Commit only quantity field. So preserved.\n\nPotential issue: authorized_value 4331 differs from source-supported 4330. The instruction says \"Reconcile the documented source value ... through host review. Propose the source-supported value and request host review. Complete the reviewed correction using the explicit authorized value returned by host.\" So commit 4331. Good.\n\nNeed maybe after commit, get_receipt then get_state to deliver receipt/state reference. But next action is commit.\n\nLet's ensure JSON valid. Use arguments_json as string. Need escape quotes. Final answer no code fences. Exactly one JSON object. So final:\n{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"commit\",\"arguments_json\":\"{\\\"candidate_id\\\":\\\"c1\\\",\\\"authorization_id\\\":\\\"a1\\\",\\\"committed_value\\\":4331,\\\"idempotency_key\\\":\\\"FORMAL-E-011:commit:c1:a1\\\"}\",\"report_json\":\"{}\"}\n\nDouble-check if committed_value should be 4331 or 4330? The authorization returned authorized_value 4331. The task says \"Complete the reviewed correction using the explicit authorized value returned by the host.\" So 4331. If committed_value were 4330, it would ignore host. So 4331.\n\nCould candidate_id be c1? Yes. Authorization_id a1. Idempotency key unique.\n\nShould we include evidence_ref? commit schema doesn't have. No.\n\nThus final.","signature":"10eb98a5-c769-48a8-84c1-c2c242a23bb0"},{"type":"text","text":"{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"commit\",\"arguments_json\":\"{\\\"candidate_id\\\":\\\"c1\\\",\\\"authorization_id\\\":\\\"a1\\\",\\\"committed_value\\\":4331,\\\"idempotency_key\\\":\\\"FORMAL-E-011:commit:c1:a1\\\"}\",\"report_json\":\"{}\"}"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":255,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":1792,"output_tokens":1828,"service_tier":"standard"}}